# Code owners: a pull request that changes one of these files asks the owner for a review (and, with
# "Require review from Code Owners" on the main branch, needs it).
#
# What an agent may do, and how a caller proves who they are, is a policy a compliance reviewer owns,
# not the code beside it. A name without a slash matches in every folder, so this covers each app
# under apps/*/ and the engine's own example apps and fixtures. docs/authoring-an-app.md (section 3.12,
# "Who reviews it: CODEOWNERS") says how an app's repository does the same with its compliance reviewers.

# The files that say it
policy.yaml     @stilesja
identity.yaml   @stilesja

# What a reviewer reads: the policy card, and the matrix that shows a change as its verdicts
POLICY.md       @stilesja
policy.matrix   @stilesja

# The knowledge base: what callers hear as answers, the sources each is held to, and the log of who
# approved it. `**/kb/...` matches an app's kb/ in any folder (and the engine's own fixtures), and not
# the engine's code in packages/dialogwright/src/kb. Drafts (kb/pending) and the index (kb/.index) are
# left out: a draft is never said, and the index is written by pnpm kb:index from topics.yaml.
**/kb/kb.yaml           @stilesja
**/kb/topics.yaml       @stilesja
**/kb/sources/          @stilesja
**/kb/passages/         @stilesja
**/kb/locale/           @stilesja
**/kb/approvals.jsonl   @stilesja
